Your teacher: Hello. I saw you using your phone during the lesson today. Can we talk for a minute?
You: Of course. {{1}}
Your teacher: You were looking at the screen while I was explaining the exercise.
You: I’m sorry. {{2}}
Your teacher: I understand, but the rule is clear. Phones must stay in your bag in class.
You: And {{3}}?
Your teacher: Yes, you can use them in the break or at lunchtime.
You: Good. {{4}}
Your teacher: Well, if the teacher asks you to use it for an activity, that is fine.
You: I see. And {{5}}?
Your teacher: This time I will only give you a warning, but next time I will call your parents.
You: {{6}}
